    "translation": "Durand died 1906. Use the Creole original; the accompanying French translation has a separate attribution question. Original includes historical racial language. Later songs and Yellow Bird adaptations are separate. The selection is the original-language text; an existing English translation is not required. Passage update (29 October 2026): Opening stanza (8 lines) and the first four lines of the last stanza. The 1923 journal transcription is unproofread OCR: three obvious slips are corrected (a full stop after “L’aut’jou” to a comma, “bell”” to “bell’”, and a missing opening « before “Ou trouvé”); the wording is unchanged. Fresh English translation by Claude (Anthropic AI); draft for editorial review.",
