    "source": "G. Cassar Pullicino’s study, University of Malta repository, quotes the manuscript-dated poem and identifies the 1901 printed heading.",
    "id": "malta",
    "contextNote": "Ġan Anton Vassallo was a pioneer of poetry in Maltese, writing when Malta was a British colony and Italian was the language of literature. He wrote this in June 1843, aged 26, after a disappointment in love, and noted in Italian that it was the last poem he would ever write in Maltese; he did write more, including the patriotic hymn “Tifħira lil Malta”.",
    "formGroup": "Poem",
    "display": {
      "title": "L-Aħħar Poeżija",
      "english": "The Last Poem",
      "creator": "Ġan Anton Vassallo",
      "language": "Maltese"
    },
    "passage": {
      "original": "Min kellu jgħidli, ja miskin jiena,\nLi dal-mant f'qalbi jien kelli nġib!\nU l-ebda fejda u l-ebda ħniena\nFl-imħabba tiegħi ma kelli nsib!\nQanpiena mbierka! fejn dari ħossok\nIkabbar fija kien qalb u ruħ;\nTħassarli 'l qalbi daż-żmien inħossok,\nIl-ħabta tiegħek tiġbidli d-dmugħ!\nLilek nistħajjel nilmaħ quddiemi\nKull fejn f'għajnejja nara s-sabiħ;\nFuqek għall-ajru inxerred kliemi\nLeħnek nistħajjel nisma' mar-riħ.\nU f'dit-taqriqa qalbi tithenna\nIżda t-taqriqa fija ma ddum;\nL-uġigħ urajha qalbi tistenna\nBil-qawwa tiegħu taqa' u ma tqum.",
      "english": "Who could have told me, poor me,\nthat I would carry this mantle of grief in my heart,\nand that no comfort and no mercy\nwould I find in my love!\nBlessed bell! where once, hearing you,\nmy heart and soul would swell within me,\nnow hearing you breaks my heart;\nyour tolling draws my tears!\nI imagine I glimpse you before me\nwherever my eyes see beauty;\nI scatter my words about you to the air,\nI imagine I hear your voice on the wind.\nAnd in this rapture my heart takes comfort,\nbut the rapture does not stay with me;\nafter it my heart awaits the pain,\nand under its force falls and does not rise.",
      "status": "draft"
    },
