    "formDetails": "Poetry",
    "genderDetails": "Man",
    "originalDate": "1845 (composition); 1913 (first printing indicated by source)",
    "editionDate": "Undated transcription; 1913 first publication",
    "description": "A sensuous night of intimacy is valued above a lifetime; the lovers part at dawn.",
    "provenance": "Original verse transcribed on Serbian Wikisource",
    "location": "Complete poem",
    "translation": "Njegoš died 1851. Titles and manuscript readings vary; compare an authoritative scan before final quotation. Original poem only; later editions’ critical apparatus is separate. The selection is the original-language text; an existing English translation is not required. Passage update (29 October 2026): 18 lines from the love scene of the poem, from the fairy’s arrival to the lovers’ kiss (Serbian Wikisource, 100% proofread). Fresh English translation by Claude (Anthropic AI); draft for editorial review.",
    "rights": "Public-domain original in the UK and other life-plus-70 jurisdictions: author died 1851. Modern editorial additions and translations are separate.",
    "source": "Source text and provenance checked 28 October 2026.",
    "id": "montenegro",
    "contextNote": "Petar II Petrović-Njegoš was both the prince-bishop who ruled Montenegro and its greatest poet. He wrote this long poem of a summer night’s love in the 1840s; he is best known for The Mountain Wreath (1847), and died in 1851, aged 37.",
    "formGroup": "Poem",
    "display": {
      "title": "Ноћ скупља вијека / Noć skuplja vijeka",
      "english": "A Night More Precious than a Lifetime",
      "creator": "Petar II Petrović-Njegoš",
      "language": "Serbian / Montenegrin"
    },
    "passage": {
      "original": "Док ево ти дивне виле лаким кроком ђе ми лети –\nзавид’те ми, сви бесмртни, на тренутак овај свети!\nХод је вилин млого дични на Аврорин када шеће,\nод сребрног свога прага над прољећем кад се креће;\nзрак је виле младолике тако красан ка Атине,\nогледало и мазање презиру јој черте фине.\nУстав’ луно, б’јела кола, продужи ми часе миле,\nкад су сунце над Инопом уставити могле виле.\nПрелесницу како видим, загрлим је ка бог вели,\nуведем је под шатором к испуњењу светој жељи.\nПри зракама красне луне, при свјећици запаљеној\nпламена се споји душа ка душици раскаљеној\nи цјеливи божествени душу с душом драгом слију.\nАх, цјеливи, божа мана, све прелести рајске лију!\nЦјелителни балсам свети најмирисни аромати\nшто је небо земљи дало на усне јој стах сисати.\nСовршенство творенија, таинствене силе боже,\nништа љепше нит’ је када нити од ње створит може!",
      "english": "When look, a lovely fairy comes flying to me with a light step —\nenvy me, all you immortals, this holy moment!\nThe fairy’s step is far more stately than Aurora’s when she walks\nfrom her silver threshold as she moves above the spring;\nthe gaze of the youthful fairy is as lovely as Athena’s,\nher fine features scorn both mirror and paint.\nStay, moon, your white chariot; prolong my precious hours,\nsince fairies once could make the sun stand still above Inop.\nAs soon as I see the enchantress, I embrace her as a god would,\nand lead her into the tent to fulfil a holy wish.\nBy the rays of the lovely moon, by a lighted candle,\na soul of flame joined a soul aglow,\nand divine kisses poured soul into beloved soul.\nAh, kisses, manna of God, pouring out all the charms of heaven!\nThe holy healing balm, the most fragrant of perfumes\nthat heaven gave the earth, I began to drink from her lips.\nPerfection of creation, mysterious power of God,\nnothing more beautiful ever was, or could be made, than she!",
      "status": "draft"
    },
