    "passage": {
      "original": "En invernales horas, mirad a Carolina.\nMedio apelotonada, descansa en el sillón,\nenvuelta con su abrigo de marta cibelina\ny no lejos del fuego que brilla en el salón.\nEl fino angora blanco, junto a ella se reclina,\nrozando con su hocico la falda de Alençón,\nno lejos de las jarras de porcelana china\nque medio oculta un biombo de seda del Japón.\nCon sus sutiles filtros la invade un dulce sueño;\nentro, sin hacer ruido; dejo mi abrigo gris;\nvoy a besar su rostro, rosado y halagüeño\ncomo una rosa roja que fuera flor de lis;\nabre los ojos; mírame, con su mirar risueño\ny en tanto cae la nieve del cielo de París.",
      "english": "In the hours of winter, look at Carolina.\nHalf curled up, she rests in the armchair,\nwrapped in her sable coat,\nnot far from the fire that glows in the drawing room.\nThe fine white angora lies beside her,\nbrushing her Alençon-lace skirt with its nose,\nnot far from the Chinese porcelain jars\nhalf hidden by a Japanese silk screen.\nWith its subtle potions a sweet sleep steals over her;\nI come in without a sound; I leave my grey coat;\nI go to kiss her face, rosy and inviting\nlike a red rose that might be a fleur-de-lis;\nshe opens her eyes; she looks at me with her smiling gaze,\nand meanwhile the snow falls from the Paris sky.",
      "status": "draft"
    },
