    "id": "palestine",
    "contextNote": "Ibrahim Tuqan wrote this as a student at the American University of Beirut in 1926, when Palestine was under British mandate. He went on to write “Mawtini” (“My Homeland”), which became a beloved Arab anthem; he died in 1941, aged 36.",
