    "source": "Linked full original text / credited edition",
    "id": "paraguay",
    "contextNote": "Ignacio Alberto Pane was a Paraguayan poet, teacher and politician who wrote in both Spanish and Guaraní, the Indigenous language spoken by most Paraguayans. Writing poetry in Guaraní was a statement of pride at a time when educated society favoured Spanish.",
